  "releaseAuthorization": {
    "state": "authorized",
    "version": "0.4.1",
    "channel": "public-alpha",
    "decision": "go",
    "authorizedBy": "@gwendall",
    "authorizedAt": "2026-08-26",
    "rationale": "Ship the 2026-08-25 review remediation as a patch on the public alpha line. Two guarantees the surfaces already advertised become true in the product: a claim now guards the terminal transition, so a third actor can no longer close work another holds, and agent integrations registered by `tasq agent install` create evidence-backed commitments, so work an agent proposes states what done looks like and closes only against an inspectable receipt. Under --json every non-zero exit now carries a typed problem contract, which is the channel agents drive. Behaviour changes are documented in CHANGELOG and are additive to the store: format 32 is unchanged, so no migration and no downgrade barrier is introduced. Independent blind-human adoption and retained multi-application dogfood remain external gates and continue to block only stable graduation, not this alpha patch."
  },
